Interoperability

bsecret speaks published standards and holds no private protocol. Any
overlay host that implements BRC-22 and BRC-24 and loads the bsecret
host module can carry a crypt and answer for it; any reader that can
check a BEEF against block headers can verify what a host answers. A
record can be delivered by a multicast plane (BRC-148) or submitted to
each host directly, and the records are the same either way. The groups
a vault is keyed to are borg's, read by borg's own packages.

